<title>SPAIN: Spain's CASA wins 7 bln pta Colombia contract.</title>
<headline>Spain's CASA wins 7 bln pta Colombia contract.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish national aircraft maker Construcciones Aeronauticas (CASA) said on Wednesday it had won a seven billion peseta contract to sell three CN-235 planes to the Colombian Airforce.</p>
<p>Casa said in a statement the three medium-size military planes would be delivered between the final months of 1997 and the beginning of 1998.</p>
<p>CASA, the smallest of the four Airbus industry partners, is owned by Spanish State holding company SEPI.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
